[tool_result] toolu_012d9B4DB2VjnYRDmRxYMFfi 1	# Usage patterns
2	
3	## Pattern 1 - Greenfield product build
4	Use when a repository is new or nearly empty.
5	
6	Workflow:
7	1. from the new project directory, run:
8	   ```
9	   bash /path/to/scaffold/scripts/bootstrap-new-project.sh [PROFILE]
10	   ```
11	   This copies agents, docs, hooks, and generates `.claude/CLAUDE.md` using the manifest profile (default: `default`).
12	2. customize `docs/SPEC.md`, `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/PHASES.md`, and `docs/PROD_REQUIREMENTS.md`
13	3. commit the scaffold-installed files. See `docs/INSTALL_LIFECYCLE.md` § "What to commit (and what to gitignore)" for the canonical list and a `.gitignore` snippet for runtime-only paths (`.claude/settings.local.json`, `.scaffold/manifest.json.lock`, `*.scaffold-tmp`).
14	4. let `project-lead` start at phase 0
15	5. require planning memos for architecture choices
16	6. iterate phase by phase until `project-complete.json`
17	
18	## Pattern 2 - Existing repo adoption
19	Use when code already exists and nee
